<issue_description>## 🎯 Objective

Create JPA entity model classes for the 5 new decision flow database views (#7918-7922), enabling type-safe data access and repository pattern usage throughout the application.

## 📋 Background

After JPA configuration (#7924), we need entity classes that map to the database views. These entities will be read-only (`@Immutable`) and follow existing CIA entity patterns.

**Entity Design Principles:**
- Immutable (read-only views)
- Composite keys where needed (party+month+committee)
- Proper JPA annotations (@Entity, @Table, @Column)
- Serializable for caching
- Lombok for boilerplate reduction (equals, hashCode, toString)

**Context from Documentation:**
- Existing pattern: `ViewRiksdagenPolitician.java`, `ViewRiksdagenParty.java`
- Package: `com.hack23.cia.model.internal.application.data.impl`

## 📊 Current State

- ✅ Database views exist (#7923)
- ✅ JPA configured (#7924)
- ❌ No entity model classes
- ❌ No repositories for data access

## ✅ Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Create 5 JPA entity classes for decision views
- [ ] Use `@Immutable` annotation (Hibernate)
- [ ] Implement composite keys using `@IdClass` or `@EmbeddedId`
- [ ] Add Spring Data JPA repositories
- [ ] Include JavaDoc with intelligence value and use cases
- [ ] Unit tests for entity mapping
- [ ] Validation: Entities load data from views correctly

